  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "omega-go publishes no fact for a string literal, so a route's path -- the first argument of r.GET(\"/users/:id\", h) -- is unreachable. Routes are identified by HTTP method plus handler name, not by URL; so are Static/StaticFile mount points and group prefixes.",
      "a handler passed as a bare identifier (r.GET(\"/x\", Healthz)) produces no reference.member, so only the qualified form (ctrl.GetUser, handlers.List) is linked by gin.route.registration; the handler itself is still declared by gin.handler.function/method.",
      "call.method carries only the selected member name, not the receiver or its package, so a middleware registered as cors.Default() is keyed on Default alone.",
      "runtime/tool execution, reflection-expanded route state and request execution are outside static scope."
    ]
  },
